demo> /help /cfg.loaded
NAME
  /cfg.loaded - Show what the config load loaded: plugins, symbols, devices.

STATUS
  stable - covered by termapy's compatibility promise

DESCRIPTION
  The table every config load reports, at startup and on a switch: one row per plugin file, symbol table and device file the load read, from the global layer and the config's own, with what each registered.  A file that failed is a row with its error.  It goes to the session log, and to the screen too when quiet_start is off.  Under MCP the profile auto-loaded on connect is a row too.  Later imports and loads (/sym.import, /dev.import, /profile.load) answer for themselves and are not added.

AVAILABLE
  TUI: yes   CLI: yes (current)   MCP: yes

SEE ALSO
  /cfg.auto, /cfg.delete, /cfg.dump, /cfg.edit, /cfg.explore, /cfg.file, /cfg.help, /cfg.icon, /cfg.info, /cfg.list, /cfg.load, /cfg.new, /cfg.rename, /cfg.show, /cfg
