demo> /help cap.text
NAME
  /cap.text - Capture serial text to a file for a timed duration.

STATUS
  stable - covered by termapy's compatibility promise

SYNOPSIS
  /cap.text <file> timeout=<dur> {mode=new|append} {echo=on|off} {cmd=<command>}

DESCRIPTION
  0 files in cap/

  Passively captures all text arriving from the device for a
  fixed duration.  Use /cap.stop to end early.

PARAMETERS
  <file>           output filename (relative to cap/ dir) (required)
  timeout=<dur>    how long to capture, e.g. 3s, 500ms (required)
  mode=new|append  file mode (default: new)
  echo=on|off      also print captured text to the terminal (default: off)
  cmd=<command>    command to send after capture starts (must be last, default: )

REQUIRED CAPABILITIES
  serial_connected - an open serial port
  capture_idle - no capture already running

AVAILABLE
  TUI: yes   CLI: yes (current)   MCP: yes

SEE ALSO
  /cap.bin, /cap.delete, /cap.dump, /cap.explore, /cap.hex, /cap.list, /cap.poll, /cap.rename, /cap.show, /cap.stop, /cap.struct, /cap.wire, /cap
