demo> /help.dev print
NAME
  /print - Print a message to the terminal.

STATUS
  stable - covered by termapy's compatibility promise

SYNOPSIS
  /print <text>

DESCRIPTION (developer)
  Write a message to the terminal output.

    Prints the argument text directly to the terminal. Useful in
    scripts for status messages or visual separators.

  Args:
      ctx: Plugin context for output.
      args: Text to print.

AVAILABLE
  TUI: yes   CLI: yes (current)   MCP: yes

SUBCOMMANDS
  /print.r    stable     Print Rich markup text (e.g. [bold red]Warning![/]).
demo> /help.dev ss.list
NAME
  /ss.list - List files in ss/, newest first, with size and age.

STATUS
  stable - covered by termapy's compatibility promise

DESCRIPTION (developer)
    List the screenshots in the config's ss/ folder, newest first, with size and age.

REQUIRED CAPABILITIES
  config_loaded - a loaded config

AVAILABLE
  TUI: yes   CLI: yes (current)   MCP: yes

SEE ALSO
  /ss.delete, /ss.explore, /ss.rename, /ss.show, /ss.svg, /ss.txt, /ss
